============================================================
1. LOGGING OBJECTIVES
============================================================
- Capture all relevant application events
- Provide traceability for admin actions
- Detect errors, anomalies, and performance issues
- Support debugging and incident response
- Maintain auditability for sensitive operations
- Enable centralized log aggregation and analysis


============================================================
2. LOGGING STANDARDS
============================================================

FORMAT
------
- All logs use structured JSON
- Required fields:
  - timestamp (ISO 8601)
  - level (INFO, WARN, ERROR)
  - message
  - request_id (if applicable)
  - user_id (if authenticated)
  - service (api, worker, db, ingress)
  - module/function name

LEVELS
------
INFO: Normal operations (startup, shutdown, successful actions)
WARN: Recoverable issues, unexpected states
ERROR: Failed operations, exceptions
CRITICAL: System-wide failures

NOISE CONTROL
-------------
- No logging of sensitive data (passwords, tokens)
- No logging of full SQL queries containing PII
- No logging of large payloads


============================================================
3. BACKEND LOGGING (FASTAPI)
============================================================

REQUEST LOGGING
---------------
- Log every request:
  - method
  - path
  - status code
  - duration
  - request_id
  - user_id (if available)

ERROR LOGGING
-------------
- Log stack traces for unhandled exceptions
- Include request_id and user_id
- Include endpoint name

AUDIT LOGGING
-------------
- All admin actions logged to audit_log table:
  - user_id
  - action
  - details
  - timestamp

DATABASE LOGGING
----------------
- Log slow queries (>200ms)
- Log connection failures
- Log migration events

SECURITY LOGGING
----------------
- Log failed logins
- Log role changes
- Log permission denials


============================================================
4. FRONTEND LOGGING (REACT)
============================================================

CLIENT-SIDE LOGGING
-------------------
- Only log non-sensitive events
- Log:
  - UI errors
  - API failures
  - Performance metrics (optional)
  - User interactions for debugging (optional)

ERROR BOUNDARIES
----------------
- Capture React component errors
- Send to backend error endpoint (optional)
- Display user-friendly fallback UI

NO SENSITIVE LOGGING
--------------------
- Never log JWTs
- Never log user passwords
- Never log PII


============================================================
5. CELERY WORKER LOGGING
============================================================

TASK LOGGING
------------
- Log task start/end
- Log task arguments (excluding sensitive data)
- Log retries
- Log failures with stack traces

QUEUE LOGGING
-------------
- Log queue delays
- Log worker health
- Log task throughput

TASK TYPES
----------
email_queue: email sends, newsletter distribution  
media_queue: image processing, thumbnail generation  
voting_queue: vote tallying, report generation  
audit_queue: admin audit events


============================================================
6. SYSTEM LOGGING (K3s + HELM)
============================================================

INGRESS LOGGING
---------------
- Log all incoming HTTP requests
- Log TLS handshake failures
- Log rate-limited requests

POD LOGGING
-----------
- Capture stdout/stderr for all pods
- Include pod name, namespace, container

NODE LOGGING
------------
- Log node health
- Log disk usage
- Log memory pressure
- Log network errors

CLUSTER EVENTS
--------------
- Log pod restarts
- Log failed deployments
- Log scaling events


============================================================
7. LOG AGGREGATION & STORAGE
============================================================

LOG AGGREGATION
---------------
- Use centralized logging (e.g., Loki, ELK, or similar)
- All services forward logs to aggregator
- Logs tagged by service and environment

RETENTION
---------
- Application logs: 30–90 days
- Audit logs: 1–3 years
- Error logs: 180 days
- Security logs: 1 year

ACCESS CONTROL
--------------
- Only admins and developers can access logs
- Audit logs restricted to GK, FS, Treasurer, Admin


============================================================
8. MONITORING & ALERTING
============================================================

METRICS
-------
- API latency
- API error rate
- Worker queue length
- Worker failure rate
- DB query performance
- DB connection pool usage
- Redis memory usage
- Pod restarts
- Node resource usage

HEALTH CHECKS
-------------
- FastAPI: /health endpoint
- Celery: worker heartbeat
- Postgres: connection test
- Redis: ping
- K3s: node health

ALERTS
------
Trigger alerts for:
- High error rate (>5% in 5 minutes)
- Slow API response (>500ms average)
- Worker queue backlog
- Pod crash loops
- DB connection failures
- Unauthorized access attempts
- Voting anomalies (duplicate votes)
- Media upload failures

ALERT CHANNELS
--------------
- Email
- Slack/Teams
- PagerDuty (optional)


============================================================
9. DASHBOARDS
============================================================

RECOMMENDED DASHBOARDS
----------------------
- API performance dashboard
- Error rate dashboard
